{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#1044","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#1044","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#1044\",\"parent_revision\":\"b6dc7e356bf8182b55fe23bf08a29c0dc3f837fc41e71d32bb7ef2ff22abfc72\",\"root_revision\":\"b6dc7e356bf8182b55fe23bf08a29c0dc3f837fc41e71d32bb7ef2ff22abfc72\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P1\\ntype: Bug\\nstatus: closed\\nadded: 2026-04-12\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nThe task-completed-kage-bunshin-reminder.cjs hook fires with the full kage-bunshin output file content injected into the context window via task-notification XML. In session d9625523 this fired 51x at avg 2,067 chars, max 10,319 chars = 105,459 chars total. The hook should inject only the task status + a path to the output file, not the full output content. Fix: cap injected content at ~500 chars and append path to output file for consumers that need full content.\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] Work matches description\\n- [ ] Plan or implementation complete\\n</div>\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-03-24T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **developer relying on this plugin**, I want to **task-notification hook: truncate output payload to prevent 105k chars/session injection** so that **the tool works correctly and reliably**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-03-24T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: vm-flightsimulator session waste audit 2026-03-24\\n- **Priority**: P1\\n- **Added**: 2026-03-24\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\\n## Groomed (2026-03-30)\\n\\n### Priority\\n\\n8/10 \u2014 Active session waste: 105K chars injected per session across 51 firings. Directly degrades orchestrator context budgets for every kage-bunshin workflow run. Fix is surgical and low-risk.\\n\\n### Impact\\n\\n- Blocks: Efficient multi-session kage-bunshin orchestration; context budget consumed by hook noise reduces room for actual task content\\n- Bottleneck: Every TaskCompleted event in a kage-bunshin session triggers unnecessary full-content injection\\n\\n### Benefits\\n\\n- Eliminates 105K+ chars of wasted context per session (measured in d9625523: 51 firings \u00d7 avg 2,067 chars)\\n- Satisfies the codebase rule \\\"check state = metadata only; action task = full content\\\"\\n- Consumers who need full session command listings can read the registry file themselves \u2014 no information is lost\\n- Hook becomes safe to fire at high frequency with negligible context cost\\n\\n### Expected Behavior\\n\\nWhen the hook fires on TaskCompleted, the orchestrator receives only: the count of active kage-bunshin sessions, and the path to the registry file. The orchestrator decides whether to read the registry file based on its own needs. No command listings, no tmux session names, no spawn.py invocations are injected.\\n\\n### Desired Structure\\n\\nThe hook emits a systemMessage containing:\\n- Session count (integer)\\n- Registry file path (absolute)\\n- One-line prompt directing the orchestrator to read the registry for full details\\n\\nThe hook does NOT emit:\\n- tmux session names or listings\\n- spawn.py command strings\\n- Any content read from files\\n- Any truncated or sliced content\\n\\n### Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n1. Run: `echo '{\\\"hook_event_name\\\":\\\"TaskCompleted\\\",\\\"session_id\\\":\\\"test123\\\"}' | node ./plugins/development-harness/hooks/task-completed-kage-bunshin-reminder.cjs` with a synthetic registry containing 2 sessions \u2014 output `systemMessage` is under 200 chars\\n2. The `systemMessage` contains the registry file path\\n3. The `systemMessage` contains the session count\\n4. The `systemMessage` does NOT contain any tmux session name strings (the `_worktree-` pattern is absent from the message)\\n5. The `systemMessage` does NOT contain any `uv run` command strings\\n6. The hardcoded `MAX_CHARS = 500` truncation block (lines 149-156 of current file) is removed\\n7. `uv run prek run --files plugins/development-harness/hooks/task-completed-kage-bunshin-reminder.cjs` exits 0\\n\\n### Resources\\n\\n| Type | Item |\\n|------|------|\\n| Prior work | /home/user/claude_skills/plugins/development-harness/hooks/task-completed-kage-bunshin-reminder.cjs (lines 129-156 \u2014 current fullMessage + truncation block to replace) |\\n\\n### Dependencies\\n\\n- Depends on: None\\n- Blocks: None\\n\\n### Effort\\n\\nSmall \u2014 the fix is localised to the message-building block (lines 129-156) of a single 165-line CJS file. Replace `fullMessage` construction and the `MAX_CHARS` truncation with a short metadata-only message. No schema changes, no other files affected.\\n\",\"digest\":\"2438528d6458345eb4905533ef6cd77656a42a70a51295fcc2f8cda023084a9b\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABVCv1EQ\"}"}